\n\
3. **Warmaster activate** - tap to make a token (from Presence of Gond).\n\
\n\
The play is: Cast Elvish Archdruid, then tap Warmaster with Gond to make tokens (triggering Warmaster for another token). Then attack with the pumped army. Opponent is at 7 life, I have massive damage.\n\
\n\
Wait, after casting Archdruid for 3 mana, I have 2 mana left. I can still tap Warmaster for a Gond token. But Warmaster would be tapped so it can't attack. But with Archdruid pumping everyone, I have plenty of damage.\n\
\n\
With Archdruid on the field: Elderleaf Mentor becomes 4/3, four tokens become 2/2s each, Warmaster becomes 3/3. If I tap Warmaster for Gond, I get a token (which triggers Warmaster for another token - wait, Warmaster will be tapped but the trigger still works since it's not a tap ability, it's an enter-the-battlefield trigger).\n\
\n\
Let me cast Archdruid first.",
